WEBVTT

01
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:10.470
Intent QA separates the application under test from the evidence workspace. The shop runs locally, while this dashboard reads the same file-backed QA artifacts used by the command line and the native agent.

02
00:00:11.153 --> 00:00:24.381
Tests stay human-readable. This YAML records intent and observable outcomes, never selectors or coordinates. The editor reuses the authoritative validator, preserves the document identity, and saves atomically only after references are valid.

03
00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:35.227
First, the stable journey. A reusable login fixture signs in without exposing credentials in evidence. The agent reaches the customer dashboard and begins the unchanged checkout specification.

04
00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:44.978
The agent opens the shopping cart and checks the visible outcome: exactly one item is present. It resolves the checkout action semantically instead of relying on a stored selector.

05
00:00:45.653 --> 00:00:54.580
At checkout, the next expectation is visible before submission. The saved test card and total are present, so the agent performs the approved payment action and continues.

06
00:00:55.253 --> 00:01:03.335
The expected confirmation appears with no error message. Cleanup runs afterward, screenshots are stored, and the functional result is classified as passed.

07
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:13.709
The result view explains the decision. Every step passed, every original expectation is preserved, and each selected accessible target is recorded beside the evidence captured during the run.

08
00:01:14.387 --> 00:01:23.995
Now the demo resets to harmless drift. Proceed to checkout has moved inside a menu and is renamed Continue to payment. The specification and its expected checkout form remain unchanged.

09
00:01:24.653 --> 00:01:37.472
The original target is absent, so the agent captures the failure, rediscovers an explicitly equivalent accessible control, retries once, and verifies the same expectation. Before-and-after evidence supports the healed classification.

10
00:01:38.153 --> 00:01:47.926
Next is a genuine functional bug. The checkout interaction still succeeds, but the application shows an order failure instead of the required confirmation. This is not eligible for healing.

11
00:01:48.587 --> 00:01:58.738
The result stays honest: functional regression. The missing confirmation is recorded as the failed observable outcome, later steps do not invent success, and the original assertion is never rewritten.

12
00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:08.654
Finally, the behavior works, but the approved confirmation design does not. The action moves ahead of the heading, and the green success treatment becomes a prominent red warning panel.

13
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:20.624
Because the functional steps passed, the explicit design checkpoint runs at its declared viewport. Concrete order and style findings, plus the actual screenshot and reference provenance, support a design regression.

14
00:02:21.287 --> 00:02:34.836
That is the complete loop: semantic YAML, reusable fixtures, native execution, conservative healing, functional and design classification, and inspectable file-backed evidence. Harmless drift recovers; real regressions remain visible.
